findings.body:
TriggeredAction now rejects automation_triggered_event_id when triggering_event is None. But act() passes the primary state-change event id for every action, and proactive triggers reach act() with triggering_event=None when bucket.last_event is None (see triggers.py around line 195, and the proactive evaluation near line 1245 that passes triggering_event=None). The Triggered state-change event is still created, so the id is non-None. The TriggeredAction constructor in act() then raises a ValidationError, nothing is published for those actions, and the exception propagates out of trigger evaluation.

::diff{file="src/prefect/server/events/schemas/automations.py" lines="772-780"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The constraint isn't needed. A link to the state-change event is valid even without a triggering event, and the existing if triggered_action.triggering_event: guards in actions.py already handle the missing-event case.

In Action.fail(), the action.triggered event was changed to related=self._resulting_related_resources, which drops the automation-triggered-event and triggering-event links that succeed() emits. action.failed still gets related_resources, so the links exist only on the failed event. The new test_failure_events_include_automation_triggered_event_link asserts the automation link on triggered_event.related, so it should fail as written.

::diff{file="src/prefect/server/events/actions.py" lines="199-203"}

Restore related=related_resources on the triggered event in fail(), matching succeed().

The updated proactive test in tests/events/server/triggers/test_service.py passes automation_triggered_event_id=parsed.automation_triggered_event_id, which is None there, so it never hits the case that breaks. None of the new tests call act() with a proactive firing whose triggering_event is None while the state-change id is set. The automation-link tests construct TriggeredAction directly with a non-None triggering_event. That gap is why the validator regression isn't caught.

::diff{file="tests/events/server/triggers/test_service.py" lines="91-97"}

Add a test that drives act() with no triggering event and asserts a TriggeredAction is published with the state-change id set.
